---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="HTTP"
  description="Understand HTTP, the protocol used for communication on the web."
>
  <article class="article container">
    <div class="eyebrow">INTERNET & NETWORKS / PROTOCOLS</div>

    <h1 class="display-title">HTTP</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      The protocol that makes communication on the web possible.
    </p>

    <div class="metadata">
      <span>CONCEPT</span>
      <span>FOUNDATIONAL TECHNOLOGY</span>
      <span>01 / INTERNET</span>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>01. Definition</h2>
      <p>
        HTTP stands for Hypertext Transfer Protocol.
        It is an application-layer protocol used for communication
        between clients and servers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>02. Why does it exist?</h2>
      <p>
        A browser needs a standardized way to request resources
        from a server. HTTP defines how those requests and responses
        are structured and exchanged.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>03. How does it work?</h2>
      <div class="code-example">
        <span class="eyebrow">REQUEST EXAMPLE</span>
        <pre><code>GET /index.html HTTP/1.1
Host: example.com
Accept: text/html</code></pre>
      </div>

      <p>
        The client sends a request. The server processes it and
        returns a response containing a status code, headers
        and potentially a message body.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>04. Related concepts</h2>
      <div class="related">
        <a href="/encyclopedia/client-server/">Client & Server ↗</a>
        <a href="/encyclopedia/json/">JSON ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>05. References</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110"
             target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            RFC 9110 — HTTP Semantics
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP"
             target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            MDN — HTTP
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <a class="back" href="/encyclopedia/">← Back to Encyclopedia</a>
  </article>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .article {
    max-width: 850px;
    padding-top: 90px;
    padding-bottom: 120px;
  }

  .article h1 {
    margin: 25px 0 10px;
    font-size: clamp(64px, 12vw, 120px);
  }

  .lead {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .metadata {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 18px;
    margin: 35px 0 65px;
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 9px;
  }

  .article section {
    margin: 55px 0;
  }

  .article h2 {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .article section p,
  .article li {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 2;
  }

  .code-example {
    margin: 25px 0;
    padding: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  pre {
    overflow-x: auto;
    color: var(--lime);
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .related {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .related a {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .article li a {
    color: var(--purple);
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 40px;
    color: var(--lime);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
</style>